    "note": "A-Engrossed version read; the Senate passed it 24-4 on 2019-04-30, and amendments made after the version read are not in the text read. Subsection (1) also makes the owner, operator or lessee liable if, after notice of stray bullets, they fail to take reasonable measures to stop more. The earlier version (not read) also let injured people sue a city or county; this version strikes that. Emergency clause in SECTION 3."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (new): A person who discharges a firearm in an active quarry or mine located on property adjacent to the Willamette River in Polk County and across the river from the City of Keizer is liable for injuries resulting from bullets that stray outside the boundaries of the property."
}